    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13029" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēmĭurgus</span></b> , or acc. to the Dor.
		form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dāmĭurgus</span></b> , i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημιουργός</span>, Dor. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δᾶμιουργός</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The chief magistrate in some of the Grecian
			states</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 32, 22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">38, 30</span></i>; <i>title of a comedy</i> of Turpilius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
